{
  "tema": 6004,
  "slug": "preterito-acciones-terminadas",
  "titulo": "The preterite for completed actions",
  "subtitulo": "Ayer surfeé dos horas.",
  "foto": "t04.jpg",
  "regla": "Use the preterite for actions that happened and finished in the past: at a specific moment, in a closed period, or as a series of events. Markers like ayer, anoche, el lunes, el año pasado and hace dos días call for it.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **preterite** (_pretérito indefinido_) tells **what happened**: an action seen as **finished**, with a beginning and an end."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It goes with time markers that point to a **closed moment** in the past:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Marker",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "**ayer**, **anoche**, **anteayer**",
              "Anoche cené tacos."
            ],
            [
              "**el lunes**, **el fin de semana**",
              "El lunes fui al doctor."
            ],
            [
              "**la semana pasada**, **el año pasado**",
              "El año pasado viajé a Oaxaca."
            ],
            [
              "**en 2020**, **en marzo**",
              "En 2020 empecé a entrenar."
            ],
            [
              "**hace** + time",
              "Hace dos días llovió."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A **closed period**, even a long one, also takes the preterite: **Viví en Ensenada cinco años** (and it's over)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A **series** of events, one after another: **Me levanté, desayuné y salí.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In Mexico the preterite is also the normal way to talk about things that just happened: **¿Ya comiste?**, **Hoy me levanté temprano.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the preterite is a photo with a date stamp. It happened, it's done."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ayer ==surfeé== dos horas en Playas.",
              "en": "Yesterday I surfed for two hours at Playas."
            },
            {
              "es": "Anoche ==vimos== una película en casa.",
              "en": "Last night we watched a movie at home."
            },
            {
              "es": "El año pasado mi hermana ==se mudó== a Mexicali.",
              "en": "Last year my sister moved to Mexicali."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Viví== en San Diego tres años.",
              "en": "I lived in San Diego for three years."
            },
            {
              "es": "El lunes ==sembré== jitomates y cilantro en el huerto.",
              "en": "On Monday I planted tomatoes and cilantro in the garden."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Llegué== a casa, ==me bañé== y ==me dormí==.",
              "en": "I got home, took a shower and fell asleep."
            },
            {
              "es": "Hace dos semanas ==gané== mi primera pelea de jiu-jitsu.",
              "en": "Two weeks ago I won my first jiu-jitsu match."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ya ==comiste==?",
              "en": "Have you eaten yet?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
